#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""./reproduce — published table -> exact pinned command.

Continuous-bench condition 1, fix 4 (methodology/continuous-bench-gap-audit-2026-08-05.md):
one entrypoint that maps each published table to the command(s) that produced it, as a thin
wrapper over the existing protocol scripts. It does not re-derive protocols; it points at
the pinned ones and checks prerequisites.

  ./reproduce                      list every table
  ./reproduce <platform> <table>   show the pinned commands + prerequisite check
  ./reproduce <platform> <table> --run [args...]
                                   execute (exec-style entries run their command list;
                                   passthrough entries forward args to the protocol script)
  ./reproduce <platform> <table> --regress
                                   condition-3 loop (exec-style entries only): re-capture
                                   into results/quality/regression/<date>-<table>/ —
                                   published reports are never clobbered — then diff
                                   against the published rows via scripts/regression_diff.py
                                   (exit 1 on a REGRESSION verdict). Typical use: bump the
                                   instrument pin, then run this.

Pins live in environment.lock.json; drivers in scripts/; raw provenance in results/raw/.
"""
